WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:02.700
- [Instructor] Let's say we're
trying to figure out what two

00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:04.840
divided by

00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:06.240
1/10 is.

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:09.380
So pause this video and see
if you can have a go at that.

00:00:09.380 --> 00:00:11.210
All right, now there's a couple of ways

00:00:11.210 --> 00:00:13.150
that we could approach this.

00:00:13.150 --> 00:00:16.240
We could just try to think of
everything in terms of tenths,

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:18.440
since we're dividing by 1/10.

00:00:18.440 --> 00:00:22.830
And so instead of two ones,
we could rewrite that two

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:26.613
as the same thing as 20/10,

00:00:26.613 --> 00:00:28.350
20/10

00:00:28.350 --> 00:00:30.141
divided by,

00:00:30.141 --> 00:00:34.283
divided by, and I could
rewrite this as 1/10.

00:00:35.710 --> 00:00:39.120
And so, if you have 20 of something

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:41.480
and if you want to divide it into groups

00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:43.040
of one of that something,

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:45.110
how many groups are you going to have?

00:00:45.110 --> 00:00:47.530
Well, you're going to have 20 groups,

00:00:47.530 --> 00:00:49.830
so this is going to be equal to 20.

00:00:49.830 --> 00:00:50.780
So that's interesting.

00:00:50.780 --> 00:00:55.780
Two divided by 1/10 is equal to twenty.

00:00:56.480 --> 00:00:58.580
Now, what if I were to take, I don't know,

00:00:58.580 --> 00:01:00.120
I'm just gonna make up another number.

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:03.760
Let's say if I were to
take seven divided by,

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:06.470
divided by 1/10.

00:01:06.470 --> 00:01:08.293
What is that going to be equal to?

00:01:09.230 --> 00:01:10.850
Well, same idea.

00:01:10.850 --> 00:01:15.270
Seven ones is the same thing as seventy

00:01:15.270 --> 00:01:16.103
tenths.

00:01:16.103 --> 00:01:18.930
And if I divide that by

00:01:18.930 --> 00:01:19.880
one

00:01:19.880 --> 00:01:21.460
tenth,

00:01:21.460 --> 00:01:23.550
well, 70 of something divided into groups

00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:27.740
of one of that something is
going to be 70 equal groups.

00:01:27.740 --> 00:01:30.770
So this is going to be equal to

00:01:30.770 --> 00:01:31.890
70.

00:01:31.890 --> 00:01:35.400
So seven divided by 1/10 is equal to 70.

00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:37.720
Two divided by 1/10 is equal to 20.

00:01:37.720 --> 00:01:39.670
You might notice a pattern.

00:01:39.670 --> 00:01:42.100
Now there's other ways that
we could've approached this.

00:01:42.100 --> 00:01:46.600
We could've said something
like two divided by 1/10

00:01:46.600 --> 00:01:50.300
is the same thing as two over 1/10,

00:01:50.300 --> 00:01:53.090
and I could write 1/10 like that.

00:01:53.090 --> 00:01:55.910
And so when you divide by a fraction,

00:01:55.910 --> 00:01:59.020
that's the same thing as
multiplying by the reciprocal.

00:01:59.020 --> 00:02:01.280
So this is the same thing as

00:02:01.280 --> 00:02:03.410
two times,

00:02:03.410 --> 00:02:04.963
two times 10.

00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:07.800
And then that pattern might
be a little bit clearer,

00:02:07.800 --> 00:02:10.530
which is going to be equal to 20.

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:12.040
When you divide by a tenth,

00:02:12.040 --> 00:02:14.680
it's the same thing as multiplying by 10.

00:02:14.680 --> 00:02:17.235
Same thing happened over here,
when we divided by a tenth,

00:02:17.235 --> 00:02:21.120
it was the same thing as
multiplying seven by 10

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:22.750
to get to 70.

00:02:22.750 --> 00:02:24.490
So what do you think is going to happen

00:02:24.490 --> 00:02:27.290
if we divide by a hundredth?

00:02:27.290 --> 00:02:29.130
So let's say I have six.

00:02:29.130 --> 00:02:33.140
And I am going to...let me make
that into a different color.

00:02:33.140 --> 00:02:34.710
So let's say I have six,

00:02:34.710 --> 00:02:37.630
and I want to divide that by

00:02:37.630 --> 00:02:39.600
a hundredth.

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:42.223
Pause this video, and see
if you can figure that out.

00:02:43.070 --> 00:02:44.770
Well, one way to approach it

00:02:44.770 --> 00:02:48.200
is we can express everything
in terms of hundredths.

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:50.680
So... I really enjoy saying hundredths.

00:02:50.680 --> 00:02:52.510
Hundredths! (chuckles)

00:02:52.510 --> 00:02:54.770
So six could be rewritten as,

00:02:54.770 --> 00:02:57.560
each whole is equal to
a hundred hundredths,

00:02:57.560 --> 00:02:59.660
so six wholes, or six ones,

00:02:59.660 --> 00:03:02.269
is going to be equal to 600 hundredths.

00:03:02.269 --> 00:03:06.602
So this is going to be
equal to 600 hundred

00:03:06.602 --> 00:03:09.680
hundredths, hundredths (chuckles),

00:03:09.680 --> 00:03:12.120
and then that's going to be divided

00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:15.920
into equal groups of one hundredth.

00:03:15.920 --> 00:03:16.963
Hundredth.

00:03:18.544 --> 00:03:20.820
So if I have 600 of
something and I'm dividing it

00:03:20.820 --> 00:03:22.850
into equal groups of
one of that something,

00:03:22.850 --> 00:03:25.070
how many equal groups am I going to have?

00:03:25.070 --> 00:03:28.570
Well, I'm going to have 600 equal groups.

00:03:28.570 --> 00:03:31.700
Now another way that we
could've approached this

00:03:31.700 --> 00:03:33.560
is we could've approached
it with fractions.

00:03:33.560 --> 00:03:37.220
We could've said hey, this
thing is the same thing

00:03:37.220 --> 00:03:38.680
as six

00:03:38.680 --> 00:03:41.020
over one hundredth,

00:03:41.020 --> 00:03:43.510
which I could express like this,

00:03:43.510 --> 00:03:48.510
which is equal to six times the
reciprocal of one hundredth.

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:53.460
So that's six times the
reciprocal of one hundredth,

00:03:53.460 --> 00:03:56.250
which is one hundred over one,

00:03:56.250 --> 00:03:59.670
or we could just write that as 100,

00:03:59.670 --> 00:04:03.280
which once again gets us to 600.

00:04:03.280 --> 00:04:05.360
So maybe you're seeing a pattern again.

00:04:05.360 --> 00:04:07.810
When you divide by a hundredth,

00:04:07.810 --> 00:04:11.310
that's equivalent to
multiplying by a hundred.

00:04:11.310 --> 00:04:13.940
When you divide by a tenth,

00:04:13.940 --> 00:04:17.650
that's the equivalent
as multiplying by 10.

00:04:17.650 --> 00:04:18.760
So I'll leave you there.

00:04:18.760 --> 00:04:20.733
I encourage you to think about that some.

